# API privacy & validation

## Privacy

- Raw Telegram messages **never** leave the browser and must **never** be stored or logged by the API.
- Persist only daily aggregates + theme + project metadata.
- Never log message content, export JSON bodies, or PII from chat exports.

## Validation

- Validate all external inputs at the boundary with **zod** (request bodies, query params, path params).
- Trust internal typed code after validation; do not re-validate everywhere.

## Payloads

- Project save payloads are aggregates + theme only; reject oversized or unexpected shapes.
